// The page's own modules (ROADMAP.md 1.4, second half): everything in src/
// that tsconfig.json does not already check, against a browser's globals
// rather than a Worker's. `npm run typecheck` runs both. Not checked yet:
// src/main.js and src/scene.js, whose hundreds of findings wait for their
// split (ROADMAP 1.2 and 1.3), and src/studio.js, which imports the vendored
// SDK — generated in Art-Talk-Back with no types of its own, so its
// JavaScript would be checked here, and it is never edited by hand. The
// modules ROADMAP 1.2 splits out of main.js (src/ui/, src/panels/,
// src/actions/) wait with it: each seam moves code as it was, so a reviewer
// can diff it line by line, and the typing pass comes after the split. (A
// checked module that imports one of the three pulls it back in: that is the
// moment to check it too.) `npm run typecheck` reports both configs' findings
// in one run, whichever fails. Same rules as tsconfig.json otherwise: JSDoc
// as the types, not strict.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["es2022", "dom", "dom.iterable"]
  },
  "files": [],
  "include": ["src/**/*.js", "src/globals.d.ts"],
  "exclude": ["src/vendor/**", "src/main.js", "src/scene.js", "src/studio.js", "src/ui/**", "src/panels/**", "src/actions/**"]
}
